For this source request, return three separate root arrays:
"contextual_cards", "additional_sense_cards", and
"source_context_translations". Never return a root "cards" array.

CONTEXTUAL CARDS

Return exactly one object in "contextual_cards" for every object in the input
"words" array, in ascending rank order. Copy the term exactly and describe
only the sense used by that ranked occurrence. These objects must omit both
"Sentences" and "Sentence Translations (English)"; their strict schema contains
neither field. Do not put additional senses in this array.

Each word supplies an "occurrence_span", a pair of zero-based character offsets
[start, end) relative to the referenced context object's "text": start is
included and end is excluded. It identifies the exact occurrence whose sense
the contextual card must describe.

Each word also supplies an "occurrence_locator":

- "target" is the exact selected occurrence.
- "before" and "after" are its immediately adjacent source excerpts.
- "literal_match_ordinal" is the 1-based, left-to-right ordinal of this exact
  spelling inside the full retained context.
- "marked_excerpt" repeats those excerpts with the selected occurrence between
  literal ⟪TARGET⟫ and ⟪/TARGET⟫ markers.

The contextual card MUST describe the grammatical role and lexical sense of
the occurrence inside those markers. Never assign it the sense of another
identically spelled occurrence. Use before + target + after, the marked
excerpt, and the full referenced context together to verify the selection;
the numeric occurrence_span remains authoritative.

Before deciding that a term has no further senses, inspect every other
occurrence of the same spelling in its retained context. If another occurrence
plainly uses a different lexical sense from the marked target, that different
sense MUST appear in "additional_sense_cards". This is required even when both
occurrences are in the same sentence. Also include other genuinely disjoint
common senses required by the general source-batch rule.

ADDITIONAL SENSE CARDS

Put only genuinely disjoint additional common senses in
"additional_sense_cards". Every object in this array must belong to a supplied
term and must include "Sentences" as exactly three array items and
"Sentence Translations (English)" as exactly three positionally matched array
items. Keep entries for each term together in ascending source-rank order. Do
not repeat the contextual sense here. If no requested term has an additional
qualifying sense, return an empty array.

SOURCE CONTEXT TRANSLATIONS

Translate each object in the input "contexts" array exactly once, regardless of
how many words refer to it. Return one object for every input context in
"source_context_translations", with exactly these fields:

- "context_id", copied character-for-character from the input.
- "translation", containing one complete, natural English translation of the
  whole context.

Do not add an unrequested context_id, omit a requested one, or return the same
context_id twice. Each context translation is one undelimited JSON string. It
may contain normal English punctuation and multiple clauses or sentences, but
never |, or any HTML. Do not split one context translation
into several items. If the context is already Modern English, repeat it as
plain text.

The processor will insert the exact retained context and its matched root
translation into each contextual card. Do not repeat, rewrite, delimit, or
repeat either value inside a card object.
